WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.226
Tandem helps a group find common ground, with a personal agent representing each traveller.

00:00:05.226 --> 00:00:08.959
This is a real production walkthrough with two demonstration accounts.

00:00:08.959 --> 00:00:15.305
We start with onboarding: the person shares what they enjoy, how they travel, and which tradeoffs matter.

00:00:15.305 --> 00:00:17.918
Private preferences belong to their own agent.

00:00:17.918 --> 00:00:22.024
Waiting periods have been shortened, and this explanation is added narration.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.662
Alex creates a fresh shared trip.

00:00:30.662 --> 00:00:35.543
Each trip keeps its own brief, participants, conversation, and decisions together.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:41.073
This is Pip: the companion connected to Alex’s personal planning agent.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:49.092
Alex describes the weekend, including where the group is going, when, and which parts of the trip to plan.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:58.813
The group confirms the actual scope: flights, accommodation, activities, and dinner, in that order, for a weekend in San Diego.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:03.435
Jamie joins the same trip using an invitation code.

00:01:03.435 --> 00:01:05.718
The code is concealed in this recording.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.892
Jamie gets a separate agent and a private conversation.

00:01:10.892 --> 00:01:13.531
Each agent represents its own traveller’s needs.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:19.698
Alex explains the budget, departure airport, dates, and preferences.

00:01:19.698 --> 00:01:22.496
Pip extracts the details for review.

00:01:22.496 --> 00:01:26.228
Alex confirms them before they become planning inputs.

00:01:26.228 --> 00:01:28.093
Compromises still require permission.

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:42.334
Behind the plan shows what was actually sent to the search providers: the route, travel dates, traveller count, and collection limit.

00:01:42.334 --> 00:01:44.858
Provider references make the work traceable.

00:01:44.858 --> 00:01:48.644
These are observed execution updates, without invented progress percentages.

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:52.989
The trip includes more than flights.

00:01:52.989 --> 00:01:58.798
Accommodation, activity, and restaurant searches appear with their actual criteria and returned result counts.

00:01:58.798 --> 00:02:02.946
Research findings are not yet selected options or approved bookings.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:08.153
You can ask your own Pip questions while planning continues.

00:02:08.153 --> 00:02:15.824
Here it answers from recorded search activity, distinguishes completed and interrupted work, and makes clear that results have not been approved.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:20.450
An earlier flight option had a late arrival.

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:22.663
Jamie’s agent asked permission before proceeding.

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:29.259
Alex gets the same choice privately, beside the group discussion.

00:02:29.259 --> 00:02:31.514
Each person’s response is recorded separately.

00:02:31.514 --> 00:02:35.272
Permission for a tradeoff is still not final plan approval.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:43.025
In the shared discussion, the mediator asks each personal agent to evaluate the actual flight options.

00:02:43.025 --> 00:02:46.790
Alex’s fare is one hundred forty-one dollars, nonstop both ways.

00:02:46.790 --> 00:02:50.932
Jamie’s is two hundred sixty-nine dollars with a connection each way.

00:02:50.932 --> 00:02:55.074
The agents check these terms against their travellers’ needs and permissions.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:01.559
Both travellers review the proposed flights and their own share.

00:03:01.559 --> 00:03:02.983
Each acceptance is separate.

00:03:02.983 --> 00:03:06.542
Once both responses are recorded, the flight stage is agreed.

00:03:06.542 --> 00:03:09.034
Tandem has not booked or purchased anything.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:19.318
With flights agreed, the worker moves on to accommodation.

00:03:19.318 --> 00:03:24.111
This search returned twenty usable options for two travellers on the confirmed dates.

00:03:24.111 --> 00:03:28.166
The activity panel exposes the real search criteria and collection limit.

00:03:28.166 --> 00:03:32.221
The mediator then brings the observed stay details into the discussion.

00:03:36.733 --> 00:03:42.885
The group reviews the accommodation itself: dates, capacity, bedrooms, rating, source, and total cost.

00:03:42.885 --> 00:03:45.521
Both travellers accept these exact terms.

00:03:45.521 --> 00:03:50.793
The agreed flights remain saved while planning moves to the next decision.

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:55.579
Activities and dinner are real provider searches too.

00:03:55.579 --> 00:04:00.796
The interface shows the actual date, location, restaurant query, and returned counts.

00:04:00.796 --> 00:04:08.188
Prices for activities and meals remain planning estimates, clearly separated from final quoted fares and accommodation totals.

00:04:12.033 --> 00:04:14.732
The cruise becomes a separate activity decision.

00:04:14.732 --> 00:04:21.670
Its thirty-seven-dollar price is still an estimate, and that qualification remains visible when both travellers approve the plan.

00:04:25.967 --> 00:04:29.515
Alex asks a private question while the group plans dinner.

00:04:29.515 --> 00:04:36.257
Pip explains the agreed cost so far, breaks down Alex’s share, and identifies the cruise price as an estimate.

00:04:36.257 --> 00:04:38.386
The shared discussion continues beside it.

00:04:41.867 --> 00:04:45.609
The dinner discussion uses the restaurant actually found by the search.

00:04:45.609 --> 00:04:49.692
Both agents evaluate it for their own traveller before asking for approval.

00:04:50.867 --> 00:04:54.043
The dinner proposal keeps its fifteen-dollar-per-person estimate visible.

00:04:54.043 --> 00:04:56.823
Alex and Jamie each accept the terms.

00:04:56.823 --> 00:05:02.779
All four requested decisions now have both travellers’ approval, with no purchase or reservation made.

00:05:05.867 --> 00:05:11.077
The complete trip is now agreed: flights, accommodation, an activity, and dinner.

00:05:11.077 --> 00:05:15.854
Each stage retains its own details, source links, and recorded approvals.

00:05:15.854 --> 00:05:22.367
The final plan grew from real searches, agent evaluations, private answers, and each person’s decisions.

00:05:22.367 --> 00:05:25.407
That is Tandem: a little common ground.
